---
description: Security rules that apply to every change
alwaysApply: true
---

- Deny by default. Every backend route declares an auth dependency; admin routes use
  `require(Permission.X)`. Ownership: `user_id` comes from the token, never the request.
- Secrets only in environment variables. Never commit `.env`, keys, service-account JSON, or real data.
- Never log tokens, refresh tokens, OTPs, TOTP codes, passwords or phone numbers.
- Passwords: Argon2id via `app/core/security.py`. Refresh tokens: store only the SHA-256 hash; rotate
  on every use; reuse revokes the session family.
- Validate all input with Pydantic/Zod. Parameterised queries only (SQLAlchemy); no string-built SQL.
- Rate-limit anything that costs money or can be brute-forced (OTP exchange, login, search, AI regenerate).
- Outbound requests: timeouts always; never fetch URLs supplied by users without an allowlist.
- Admin mutations check `Origin`; cookies are `__Host-`, HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict.
- Changes to auth, sessions, permissions or migrations need a second review of the diff before merge.
